   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (14) as a formal conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Anyone who still opposes the station clearly does not care about science education at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Because a station would improve learning in several subjects at a modest yearly cost, the department should install one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In conclusion, weather is important, and everyone should pay closer attention to it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"The school should also build a greenhouse beside the station for the biology classes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because a station would improve learning in several subjects at a modest yearly cost, the department should install one.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and draws on both the learning evidence and the cost reasoning in sentences (10) and (11). The general statement about weather drops the writer's actual position.$q$, 'draft', 'd09558db-650a-5eef-a3cc-7d5ab167ec1a')
