  ('105cabe1-6338-5e87-8290-42c9c90055b7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A reader might say the score increase in sentence (5) could have happened for other reasons. Which sentence, added after sentence (5), would best answer that concern?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Fairlow's teachers made no other changes to the earth science course during those years.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many students say they enjoy learning about storms, floods and hurricanes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-generalization"},{"text":"The regional earth science exam is given to every tenth grader each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"},{"text":"Fairlow High is well known throughout the region for its strong athletic teams.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Fairlow's teachers made no other changes to the earth science course during those years.$q$, $q$If nothing else in the course changed, the station becomes a more likely reason for the higher scores, which strengthens the reasoning behind sentence (5). The detail about when the exam is given explains the test but does nothing to rule out other causes.$q$, 'draft', 'd09558db-650a-5eef-a3cc-7d5ab167ec1a')
