-- Passage wg10-argument-writing-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('101d4c66-b8d7-5ec3-9cc9-968e616112bd', 'wg10-argument-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Protected Lanes on Tamsin Avenue$q$, $q$(1) Tamsin Avenue connects Harrow Middle School, Lindell High School and the public pool, yet cyclists on the avenue share a narrow lane with cars and delivery trucks. (2) Bikes are a topic that many people have opinions about. (3) A city traffic count last fall found that about 340 students ride bicycles along the avenue on a typical school day. (4) During the same year, the police department recorded eleven collisions between cyclists and vehicles on the avenue, more than on any other street in town. (5) In the town of Bellmere, which added curb-separated bike lanes to a busy street in 2021, collisions involving cyclists dropped by 60 percent over the next two years. (6) Bellmere is also famous for its annual pumpkin festival.

(7) Shop owners in the Riverside district worry that removing street parking to make room for the lanes would drive away customers. (8) Their concern is understandable, since many of them depend on drivers who stop for quick errands. (9) A study of 40 small businesses on Bellmere's redesigned street found that sales held steady or rose at 34 of them. (10) The city could also turn the empty lot behind the post office into a small parking area to replace the lost spaces.

(11) Protected lanes on Tamsin Avenue would make daily trips safer for hundreds of students. (12) Bikes are fun, and that is about all there is to say.$q$, 'draft')
