insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8bc39fcc-09ec-5061-a577-6aac479d141c', 'wg10-argument-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Pitch Limits in the Lakemont League$q$, $q$(1) The Lakemont Youth Baseball League, which serves players ages 11 to 15, currently places no limit on how many pitches a player may throw in a game. (2) The league should adopt a rule limiting each pitcher to 85 pitches per game and requiring rest days after any outing over 50 pitches. (3) Arm injuries in young pitchers often develop slowly, as repeated stress strains muscles and growth plates that are still developing. (4) A five-year study of 1,200 youth pitchers by the Northgate Sports Medicine Clinic found that players who regularly threw more than 85 pitches in a game were three times as likely to need elbow treatment. (5) Last season, two Lakemont pitchers missed the playoffs because of sore elbows, and one needed months of physical therapy. (6) The league's uniforms were redesigned in navy and gold last season.

(7) Some coaches argue that pitch limits would force teams to use weaker pitchers in close games, making competition less fair. (8) It is true that a limit would change how coaches plan their games. (9) Leagues in neighboring Carroway County adopted the same limits four years ago. (10) Their coaches now train six or seven pitchers per team instead of three, and the share of close games, those decided by two runs or fewer, has stayed about the same.

(11) Coaches who complain about pitch counts are just being selfish. (12) Protecting young arms now means more players will still be able to pitch in high school and beyond.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
