   $q$The claim in sentence (2) has two parts, but the evidence supports mainly the pitch limit. Which sentence would best support the second part, the required rest days?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many professional pitchers ice their arms carefully after every game they pitch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"},{"text":"Rest days would also give young players more time to finish their homework.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-benefit"},{"text":"Some parents say their children enjoy pitching more than playing any other position.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-evidence"},{"text":"The same Northgate study found that pitchers who rested two days after long outings reported elbow pain far less often.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The same Northgate study found that pitchers who rested two days after long outings reported elbow pain far less often.$q$, $q$The correct choice gives evidence about rest days for youth pitchers, the exact part of the claim that lacks support. Icing by professional pitchers concerns a different practice and a different age group.$q$, 'draft', '8bc39fcc-09ec-5061-a577-6aac479d141c')
