  ('bc4f33cf-d10b-5702-888b-8e8c9bc4d08a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (11) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To conclude, technology changes so quickly that no one can predict the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Because repairable laptops pay for themselves within two years and cut waste, the district should choose them in March.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The district should also buy every teacher a brand new tablet next year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Anyone who prefers the old laptops is wasting the district's money on purpose.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because repairable laptops pay for themselves within two years and cut waste, the district should choose them in March.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and draws on the savings and waste evidence. The current sentence (11) gives up the writer's position, and the choice about predicting the future is just as vague.$q$, 'draft', '281e851b-ca46-5e9b-a469-57b06e7317bb')
