values
  ('7fcbb54e-2b55-56c4-9513-9816edf132c5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (2) that distinguishes the claim from an alternate approach. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some students prefer to write their essays by hand instead of typing them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Repairable laptops are the single most important issue facing the district today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"Laptops have become a necessary tool in nearly every classroom in the district.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Buying cheaper laptops and replacing them often may seem simpler, but it costs more over time.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Buying cheaper laptops and replacing them often may seem simpler, but it costs more over time.$q$, $q$The correct sentence names the alternate approach, buying cheaper laptops, and explains why the writer's plan differs from it. The statement about laptops in classrooms is true but does not set the claim apart from any other option.$q$, 'draft', '281e851b-ca46-5e9b-a469-57b06e7317bb')
