insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1b5b026f-499d-58f0-890c-74bbe3061ad8', 'wg10-argument-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Swim Lessons at Pell Harbor High$q$, $q$(1) Pell Harbor sits on a bay with four public beaches, yet many students at Pell Harbor High cannot swim the length of a pool. (2) Swimming is something a lot of people do in the summer. (3) A fall survey by the physical education department found that 31 percent of ninth graders could not swim 25 meters without stopping. (4) The town's lifeguard captain reported that most of the rescues at local beaches last summer involved teenagers. (5) Pell Harbor High already has access to the community center's indoor pool, which sits empty most weekday mornings. (6) The pool was built in 1974 and has eight lanes.

(7) Some parents worry that a swimming unit would take time away from other activities, such as team sports and fitness testing. (8) The department could shorten the volleyball unit from six weeks to three, a change the physical education teachers themselves have proposed. (9) Other parents are concerned that students who already swim well would be bored. (10) Strong swimmers could instead earn certification in basic water rescue, a skill that could lead to summer lifeguard jobs.

(11) So basically, swimming is cool and the school should do it.$q$, 'draft')
