  ('7405e364-b78f-582e-aee0-606950399a31', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (11) as a formal conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Parents who object to the plan clearly do not care about their children's safety.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Overall, safety should always be the top priority for everyone in every situation.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"The school should also start a sailing club for students who enjoy the bay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"By using an empty pool and a shorter volleyball unit, the school could teach every student to swim at little cost.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By using an empty pool and a shorter volleyball unit, the school could teach every student to swim at little cost.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion follows from the evidence and the answers to both objections. The sentence about parents attacks people who disagree instead of keeping an objective tone.$q$, 'draft', '1b5b026f-499d-58f0-890c-74bbe3061ad8')
