  ('ff514e24-0561-5f64-abbc-6fb25cbcdb2a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (4) is less precise than sentence (3). Which revision would make sentence (4) the strongest evidence for the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The town's lifeguard captain believes that swimming is the best form of exercise for teenagers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-evidence"},{"text":"The town's lifeguard captain reported that 19 of the 27 rescues at local beaches last summer involved swimmers ages 13 to 18.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The town's lifeguard captain, who has worked at the beaches for years, said rescues are always stressful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"},{"text":"The town's lifeguard captain reported that the local beaches were very crowded last summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The town's lifeguard captain reported that 19 of the 27 rescues at local beaches last summer involved swimmers ages 13 to 18.$q$, $q$Exact numbers showing that most rescues involved teenagers make the danger concrete and connect it to students. The captain's opinion about exercise is not evidence that students need swimming instruction for safety.$q$, 'draft', '1b5b026f-499d-58f0-890c-74bbe3061ad8')
