  ('ae67ad7d-6c39-5ff8-b2f0-2d88a3854384', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (9) answers the idea that forests have always changed, but the cost raised in sentence (8) is answered only indirectly. Which sentence, added after sentence (10), would best address the cost directly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Healthy hemlocks can live for several hundred years if they are protected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-off-point"},{"text":"Many people in town enjoy fishing for brook trout each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The commission's land fund can cover the treatment for five years, by which time the beetle is expected to be ready.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Money should never matter when the future of nature is at stake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-assertion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The commission's land fund can cover the treatment for five years, by which time the beetle is expected to be ready.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows that the $18,000 yearly cost can be paid for the limited time the treatment is needed. Saying money should never matter dismisses the objection instead of answering it with evidence.$q$, 'draft', 'df3f57e2-4c90-55ba-8db2-54649a4d7cd1')
